      "content": "The walls are only real because you're holding onto them with fear, and you can't build them out of thin air if you don't want to. You don't need to change everything to feel safe; you just need to let go of the idea that you have to be perfect to deserve peace. It's okay to stop everything for a moment, but don't let that silence convince you that there's no other way out.",
